<title>USA: CONMED buys product line from C.R.Bard unit.</title>
<headline>CONMED buys product line from C.R.Bard unit.</headline>
<dateline>UTICA, N.Y. 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>CONMED Corp said Thursday it had signed an agreement to buy the Yankauer, Poole, Frazier and Sigmoidoscopic and connecting tubing surgical suction instrument product line from Davol Inc, a subsidiary of C.R. Bard.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>CONMED said the deal, which does not include Davol's performance irrigation product line, is expected to close June 30.</p>
<p>The products have sales of about $25 million, CONMED said.</p>
